<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Payment auto-refunded — <%= @payment_intent_id %></title></head>
<body style="font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px;">
  <h2 style="color: #B91C1C;">↩️ Payment auto-refunded</h2>
  <p>A buyer paid but the gift card could not be created (permanent fulfillment failure), so the charge was refunded in full automatically. No gift card exists for this payment.</p>

  <table cellpadding="6" style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; background: #f9fafb; border-radius: 8px;">
    <tr><td><strong>Stripe PaymentIntent:</strong></td><td><code><%= @payment_intent_id %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Stripe refund ID:</strong></td><td><code><%= @refund_id %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Amount refunded:</strong></td><td><%= @amount_formatted %></td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Failure reason:</strong></td><td><code><%= @reason %></code></td></tr>
  </table>

  <p style="margin-top: 24px;">
    No action is required for the buyer. If this reason keeps recurring
    (e.g. <code>purchase_limit_exceeded</code>, <code>merchant_inactive</code>),
    investigate the upstream cause.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="https://dashboard.stripe.com/payments/<%= @payment_intent_id %>"
       style="display: inline-block; background: #FCA50F; color: #0D2F32; padding: 10px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: bold;">
      Open in Stripe Dashboard
    </a>
  </p>
</body>
</html>
